                                "sense_id": "b634f975-0539-3f2b-9b0b-a90c64d14836",
                                "text": "Men are mistaught many things: that violence and control of others are acceptable, that they are strong and therefore entitled to be violent. Similarly they are taught that they are not victims; that they can and should take care of themselves. For gay men, this heritage can lead to violence in their relationships and denial about their victimization."
